{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And Yair son of Menasheh.</b> He is called by his mother's name, even though he is from the tribe of Yehudah, for thus it is written: ״for Chezron took the daughter of Makhir״ and begot from her Seguv, and Seguv begot Yair, who had cities in the cities of Gil'ad. A parallel to this is found in Ezra, where priests are called by the name of Barzilai the Gil'adi. There is no opening for the opponent to object how Yair took an inheritance with another tribe, for the land of Canaan is what is divided among the tribes, and not the land of the Emori — the land of Sichon and Og, which is across the Jordan eastward." "<b>And he called them Havot Yair.</b> Since he was killed in the war of Ai, it is written here that he did so before the conquest of the land, and called them by his name, to make his name remembered upon them for his valor."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:31.694684049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}